ystematic error, and a held phase sign, thresholding the sample mean of S at zero has one-sided error <=exp(-n v\u00b2/4). Neither a port threshold nor this iid rate applies without phase calibration, or to unmodeled common run-to-run drifts.","no_go":"On any finite coordinate transcript H->-H multiplies every retained physical amplitude by (-1)^t when each coherent history has t Hadamards, including the reference, apparatus and calibrator. Initial integer coordinates up to a scalar, signed permutations and coordinate masks preserve integer numerators; complete cylinder probabilities, conditioning and positive coarse graining are rational and identical. Different classical adaptive branches can have different t. This extends to equal parity of H depths after clearing dyadic denominators. A locally referenced approximate phase prepared by such coordinates obeys the same no-go when records include the reference.","gauge":"Treat the black-box bypass at a layer as U(sigma,phi)=diag(sigma H,exp(i phi) I) on the addressed subspaces. The simultaneous change (sigma,phi)->(-sigma,phi+pi) sends U to -U and full H to -H. Any fixed invocation on the whole state has a common sign; arbitrary coordinate routing, feedback, tomography, fresh copies or same-machine calibration made only from this menu preserve every transcript. A further coherently controlled invocation that can itself be skipped needs a separately specified phase. A classical random common sign can also be latent across repeated trials.","visibility":"For the original physical M=8 placement, let Gamma be the complex normalized shallow/deep marker overlap including phase. For odd strides E[S|d]=sigma Re(Gamma) cos(pi d/4); for even d it is cos(pi d/4). A known positive Re(Gamma)>=v gives opposite unit-stride predictions separated by >=v/sqrt(2) in plus probability. Re(Gamma)=0 makes all those unit-stride means 1/2. Complete orthogonal labels erase the interference; a purely imaginary Gamma has zero real contrast for these real reads. Populations alone do not measure the overlap. A single global field embedding conjugates all supplied algebraic gates; here the nuisance phase is an independently variable physical parameter.","synchronized_control":"Supply a fresh spectator bit and H-pair every otherwise idle mode on it at each matched layer. Numerator depth three for all modes. Even shallow sites end with spectator (0+1)/sqrt(2), odd deep sites carry 0. For T the unconditional bright probability is 3/4 under either embedding, marker-zero yield 3/4 and conditional bright 5/6. These are properties of the synchronized integer ensemble including its calibrator. A permanent deep marker of the original bypass versus orthogonal shallow marker gives 1/2.","phase_test":"Additional calibrated gate diag(1,exp(i phi)) on two equal-H-depth reference paths gives plus probability (1+cos(phi))/2, independent of sigma. If this separately addressable sensor is validated to have the same phase as the bypass and the route-marker overlap is real, known and positive, its contrast and the unit-stride bypass contrast give a relative sign when cos(phi) differs from zero. An interpretation as an embedding test needs an independently held acted/idle phase and a held physical T. Without establishing phase transfer or visibility the nuisance can absorb the sign. A reference can be on the same machine; no supplied empirical comparison is asserted.","source_context":["Finite_clock_purity.md","Native_preparations_and_probability_embeddings.md","check_clock_galois_support.py"]}
